Third-party code
----------------

gpuix
  The renderer (crates/pumi-gpuix) and its React bindings (runtime/app/native,
  runtime/app/react) are forked from gpuix, "React and Solid for GPUI":
  https://github.com/remorses/gpuix. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (LICENSE-APACHE). Changed for pumi.

GPUI and Zed
  GPUI (vendor/gpui, vendor/gpui_linux, vendor/gpui_macos, vendor/gpui_windows, and the git
  dependencies named in Cargo.toml) is part of Zed, https://github.com/zed-industries/zed, and
  comes from gpuix's fork at https://github.com/remorses/zed. Copyright Zed Industries, Inc.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (vendor/gpui/LICENSE-APACHE). Changed for pumi.

  crates/pumi-gpuix/src/custom_elements/input.rs follows GPUI's input example
  (crates/gpui/examples/input.rs, Apache-2.0).

  The macOS editing shortcuts in src/term/keys.rs (MAC_EDITING) are those of Zed's terminal keymap
  (assets/keymaps/default-macos.json). Copyright Zed Industries, Inc. Licensed under the GNU
  General Public License, version 3 or later.

  Several parts of pumi's interface are modelled on Zed's: its panes and their tab strips, its
  side bar and title bar, and how it updates itself. They are written for pumi; their
  comments say "as Zed's".

Comet
  Text selection and painting in crates/pumi-gpuix/src/text (mod.rs, selection.rs, paint.rs),
  the theme tokens in crates/pumi-gpuix/src/theme.rs, and the editing behaviour of
  crates/pumi-gpuix/src/custom_elements/input.rs are ported from Comet,
  https://github.com/zeronsh/comet. Copyright (c) 2026 Wing. Licensed under the MIT License
  (crates/pumi-gpuix/LICENSE-COMET). Changed for pumi.

libghostty-vt and Ghostty
  The terminal emulator, and its key and mouse encoders, are libghostty-vt, the terminal
  emulation library of Ghostty (https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty, MIT License), used through
  its Rust binding libghostty-rs (https://github.com/uzaaft/libghostty-rs, MIT or Apache-2.0).
  It is a build dependency, fetched from its repository at a pinned commit; its build fetches
  Ghostty's sources at the commit it names. Several terminal settings take their names and
  behaviour from Ghostty's.

iTerm2 Color Schemes
  runtime/app/app/theme/terminal/themes.json is from iTerm2-Color-Schemes,
  https://github.com/mbadolato/iTerm2-Color-Schemes. Copyright (c) 2011 to Present Mark Badolato.
  Licensed under the MIT License (runtime/app/app/theme/terminal/LICENSE).

Lucide
  The icons in assets/icons are from Lucide, https://lucide.dev. Licensed under the ISC License,
  with portions from Feather under the MIT License (assets/icons/LICENSES).

The Rust and JavaScript dependencies named in Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and the package.json files
are under their own licenses.
